  "text": "Classic Neapolitan ice cream is a delightful combination of three traditional flavors: **vanilla**, **chocolate**, and **strawberry**. Here's a simple and delicious recipe you can follow at home:\n\n---\n\n### \ud83c\udf66 **Classic Neapolitan Ice Cream Recipe**\n\n#### **Ingredients** (Makes about 2 quarts / 2 liters)\n\n**For the Base:**\n- 2 cups (480 ml) whole milk  \n- 1 cup (240 ml) heavy cream  \n- 3/4 cup (60 g) sugar  \n- 1 teaspoon vanilla extract  \n- 1/4 teaspoon salt  \n\n**For the Flavors:**\n- **Vanilla Ice Cream:**\n  - 1/2 cup (115 g) sugar  \n  - 1 vanilla bean, split and scraped (or 1 teaspoon vanilla extract)  \n\n- **Chocolate Ice Cream:**\n  - 1/2 cup (115 g) unsweetened cocoa powder  \n  - 1/2 cup (115 g) sugar  \n  - 1/2 cup (120 ml) heavy cream  \n  - 1/4 cup (60 ml) whole milk  \n  - 1/2 teaspoon salt  \n  - 1/2 teaspoon vanilla extract  \n\n- **Strawberry Ice Cream:**\n  - 1 (14 oz / 400 g) can crushed strawberries (or 1.5 cups fresh strawberries, pureed)  \n  - 1/2 cup (100 g) sugar  \n  - 1/4 cup (60 ml) heavy cream  \n  - 1/2 teaspoon vanilla extract  \n\n---\n\n#### **Instructions:**\n\n**1. Make the Base:**\n- In a large bowl, combine the milk, heavy cream, sugar, vanilla extract, and salt. Whisk until the sugar is dissolved.  \n- Churn this mixture in an ice cream maker according to the manufacturer's instructions. Typically, this takes 20\u201330 minutes.  \n- Chill the churned base in the freezer for at least 2 hours before adding flavors.\n\n**2. Make the Flavors:**\n- **Vanilla:** In a separate bowl, combine the sugar, vanilla bean (or extract), and 1 cup of the base. Whisk well.  \n- **Chocolate:** In another bowl, mix the cocoa powder, sugar, heavy cream, milk, salt, and vanilla. Whisk until smooth.  \n- **Strawberry:** In a third bowl, combine the crushed strawberries, sugar, heavy cream, and vanilla. Whisk until well mixed.\n\n**3. Fold the Flavors:**\n- Once the base is chilled, fold in the three flavored mixtures into the base.  \n- Continue churning for another 10\u201315 minutes, or until the mixture is firm but still soft.\n\n**4. Freeze:**\n- After churning, transfer the ice cream to an airtight container.  \n- Freeze for at least 2\u20133 hours, or until fully set.\n\n**5. Serve:**\n- Let the ice cream sit at room temperature for 5\u201310 minutes before serving for the best texture.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udca1 Tips:\n- For extra richness, you can use a mix of heavy cream and whole milk.\n- If you want a swirl effect, use a spoon to swirl each flavor together before freezing.\n- Store in the freezer for up to 1 month.\n\nEnjoy your homemade Neapolitan ice cream! \ud83c\udf66\ud83c\udf68\ud83c\udf53\ud83c\udf6b\u2728",
